# The producer bounds of the standard-old family for the staged presentation

Manuscript `diophantine_zq.tex`, tex 2720, 2729–2741, 2836–2838, 4385–4414, 4520–4550.

The contributor's `standardOld_producerBounds` (one `B`, vanishing outside `[0, 3]`, for the
standard-old stage Selmer family over `Acoef i`) takes the hypotheses `hTor`, `h410`, `hlcd`,
`hloc`, `hglob`, `hK`, `hSfin`, `h2`. For lane RC32's staged presentation `P` at the stage `s`:

* `hTor` (PROVED): `E[2^i]` rational over `K_{S₀ s}` at every `i`, from `P.full s`;
* `hK` (PROVED, `isTotallyComplex_of_sqrt`): `K = ℚ(√k)` with `k < 0` is totally complex;
* `h2` (PROVED): the places above `2` lie in `P.S s`, from `P.full s`
  (`h2_of_hasFullTwoTorsion_proof`);
* `hSfin` (PROVED from named inputs): `P.S s = P.S₀ s ∪ range P.pl` is finite when `P.S₀ s` is
  finite (`hS0fin`, a formalization requirement: the text's supports are finite, tex 2729–2741)
  and the chain has finitely many indices (`[Finite P.ι]`);
* `h410`, `hlcd`, `hloc`, `hglob` (named PRINTs, as in the contributor's statement: Milne,
  *Arithmetic Duality Theorems*, I.4.10(c), I.1.12 with I.1.6(b), I.2.1/I.2.3, I.4.15).

**`standardOld_producerBounds_staged`** (PROVED): the producer bounds for the staged
presentation's standard-old family, for the old-condition data `Bv`, `label`, `m`, `ι`, `hι`
(the data matching the presentation's conditions are chosen with the degreewise identification).

Kinds: PROVED.
-/

